HST Office on Windows: own ProgIDs for the legacy StarOffice 6 / OpenOffice.org 1 formats too.

The MSI still registered the legacy ProgIDs under LibreOffice's names (soffice.StarWriterDocument.6,
soffice.StarCalcTemplate.6, soffice.StarConfigFile.6, ... and their version-independent CurVer
keys) for .sxw/.sxc/.sxi/.sxd/.sxm/.sxg/.stw/.stc/.sti/.std and the old config/basic files. With
both suites installed, the one installed last owned these open commands, and uninstalling either
deleted the keys the other used.

- scp2: every soffice.Star* ProgID is HSTOffice.Star* (the keys, CurVer, the .ext defaults, the
  OLE class ProgID/VersionIndependentProgID values and the Capabilities FileAssociations).
- The shell extension's self-registration table uses the same names.
- Unchanged on purpose: the OLE storage type names embedserv writes into documents
  (soffice.Star*Document.6), and the OLE class IDs, which documents store.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).

